      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The concept of \"equal chance\" in a lottery is a false equivalence when dealing with housing scarcity and economic disparity. True equity means providing what people *need* to achieve a baseline standard of living, not just giving everyone a coin flip. Therefore, an income-based system is the only truly equitable policy because it actively corrects for systemic economic disadvantages.",
      "source": "target",
